[95.478115, "o", "stdout\":\"APP0000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\\nAPP0000002APPRO\\n001 00002316.70 00002291.67 00000025.03 0000004974.97\\n002 00002316.70 00002280.19 00000036.51 0000004938.46\\n003 00002316.70 00002263.46 00000053.24 0000004885.22\\n004 00002316.70 00002239.06 00000077.64 0000004807.58\\n005 00002316.70 00002203.47 00000113.23 0000004694.35\\n006 00002316.70 00002151.58 00000165.12 0000004529.23\\n007 00002316.70 00002075.90 00000240.80 0000004288.43\\n008 00002316.70 00001965.53 00000351.17 0000003937.26\\n009 00002316.70 00001804.58 00000512.12 0000003425.14\\n010 00002316.70 00001569.86 00000746.84 0000002678.30\\n011 00002316.70 00001227.55 00001089.15 0000001589.15\\n012 00002316.70 00000728.36 00001588.34 0000000000.81\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[107.915356, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01W1ssU2AtwWKcmJm2obCHQK\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The program works. However, looking at the output for the second record, the interest rate (5.50%) is being applied incorrectly. The loan amount is 5000 and the first payment interest should be much smaller. Let me check - the rate 00550 should be 5.50%. But looking at my calculations, it appears the rate parsing or the TERM interpretation is wrong. Let me check the input more carefully:\\n\\n- Record 2: LOAN=5000, PROPERTY=4000, DOWN=3500, TERM=01, RATE=00550\\n\\nWait, the TERM is 01 (1 year = 12 months) and the RATE format is 9(3)V9(2) meaning 00550 = 005.50 = 5.50%.\\n\\nBut there's an issue - the down payment (3500) is less than 15% of property value (4000 * 0.15 = 600), so record 2 should actually be approved. But looking more closely: 3500 > 600 so it's approved correctly.\\n\\nHowever, looking at the first record:\\n- LOAN=2000000000, PROPER"]
[107.915505, "o", "TY=3500000000, DOWN=500000000, TERM=20, RATE=00550\\n- MIN_DOWN = 3500000000 * 0.15 = 525000000\\n- DOWN=500000000 < 525000000, so DENIED - correct!\\n\\nBut record 2 calculation issue - with loan of 5000, rate of 5.50% annually, and 12 months:\\n- monthly rate = 5.50 / 1200 = 0.00458333\\n- payment should be around 428, not 2316\\n\\nThe issue is that the rate field 9(3)V9(2) is being read as 550.00 instead of 5.50. Let me fix the parsing:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":542,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":22242,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":542,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b29978c-b06c-4817-86b1-40feacb81a85\",\"uuid\":\"4ade5412-86c5-4cb2-b06a-be2350b26108\"}\r\n"]
