[184.362666, "o", "stdout\":\"APP0000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\\nAPP0000002APPRO\\n001 00000429.18 00000022.92 00000406.26 0000004593.74\\n002 00000429.18 00000021.05 00000408.13 0000004185.61\\n003 00000429.18 00000019.18 00000410.00 0000003775.61\\n004 00000429.18 00000017.30 00000411.88 0000003363.73\\n005 00000429.18 00000015.42 00000413.76 0000002949.97\\n006 00000429.18 00000013.52 00000415.66 0000002534.31\\n007 00000429.18 00000011.62 00000417.56 0000002116.75\\n008 00000429.18 00000009.70 00000419.48 0000001697.27\\n009 00000429.18 00000007.78 00000421.40 0000001275.87\\n010 00000429.18 00000005.85 00000423.33 0000000852.54\\n011 00000429.18 00000003.91 00000425.27 0000000427.27\\n012 00000429.18 00000001.96 00000427.22 0000000000.05\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[192.777731, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01SSP1du5dPRZxS1AVDMAtF7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The program is now working correctly. Let me verify the calculation is accurate:\\n\\nFor record 2:\\n- Loan = 5000\\n- Rate = 5.50% annually\\n- Term = 1 year = 12 months\\n- Monthly rate = 5.50 / 1200 = 0.00458333\\n- Monthly payment = 5000 * 0.00458333 / (1 - (1.00458333)^(-12))\\n- = 22.9167 / 0.053437 = 429.04 (approximately)\\n\\nThe output shows 429.18 which is close (small rounding differences are expected). The payment schedule shows decreasing interest and increasing principal as expected for an annuity payment.\\n\\nLet me verify the first record denial is correct:\\n- Property value = 3,500,000,000\\n- Min down = 3,500,000,000 * 0.15 = 525,000,000\\n- Down payment = 500,000,000 < 525,000,000 → DENIED ✓\\n\\nThe program works correctly. Let me also verify line lengths don't exceed 80 characters:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usa"]
